# Whiteboard & Discrete A4 Pages Rules

- Self-Contained Canvas Engine (NO Excalidraw): The whiteboard is a custom `<canvas>` renderer with our own tools, elements, and hit-testing. Do NOT add or depend on `@excalidraw/*` or any external whiteboard library.
- Discrete A4 Pages:
  - Each page is an independent A4 canvas of `794px × 1123px` (CSS pixels), stacked vertically as discrete pages.
  - Canvases are DPR-aware: back the canvas at `PAGE_W * dpr` × `PAGE_H * dpr` and `ctx.scale(dpr, dpr)` so drawing stays sharp on high-density / iPad screens.
  - The drawing canvas is transparent and layered on top of a squared grid background (the grid is the page background, strokes render above it).
- Touch & Tablet UI: Custom toolbars must be draggable floating panels with a toggle button so they do not block iPad writing.
- Image Pasting: Convert pasted/uploaded files to a Base64 DataURL via `FileReader` and draw them onto the canvas. Never use the native File System Access API.
- RTL Isolation: The surrounding UI stays RTL; the canvas drawing surface operates in its own coordinate space independent of text direction.
